      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-251177",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a normal population with mean $\u03bc = 15$ and unknown variance. An independent random sample is drawn from the population, and it is found that approximately $68%$ of the data in the sample have a value between $10$ and $20$. Using the empirical rule for the normal distribution, find an estimate of the population variance."
