      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-251178",
      ":question/problem": "A hospital director wants to estimate the population variance of the number of serious emergencies per day in his hospital. He knows that the population mean is $\u03bc = 19$ serious emergencies per day, and on $95%$ of the days over the past five years, the number of serious emergencies ranged from $15$ to $23$ per day. Assuming that the number of emergencies in a randomly selected day is normally distributed, find an estimate of the population variance."
